CAFE is a named stack. Each letter has one job.

[Maxwell Brown](https://github.com/IMax153) coined the name; [Justin Bennett](https://github.com/just-be-dev) spread it with his template on 8 October 2026. That day, [Devin Jameson](https://github.com/devinjameson), Maxwell and [Sam Goodwin](https://github.com/sam-goodwin) streamed a CAFE build, and [Sebastian Lorenz](https://github.com/fubhy) wrote the explainer people share.

| Letter | Part | Job |
| --- | --- | --- |
| C | Cloudflare | Runs the app: Workers, Durable Objects, storage, static assets. |
| A | Alchemy | Declares the cloud resources as an Effect program. |
| F | Foldkit | Draws the UI with the Elm Architecture on Effect. |
| E | Effect | Does the typed work between the UI and the cloud. |

A request follows one path. The [Alchemy](/skills/learn-alchemy) Stack declares every box on it.

```text
┌─ Alchemy Stack ──────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                  │
│  Foldkit app (browser)                           │
│      │  HTTP or RPC, typed by a shared schema    │
│      ▼                                           │
│  Worker (Effect)                                 │
│      │                                           │
│      ▼                                           │
│  Durable Object or storage                       │
│                                                  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

The browser and the Worker import the same schemas. Alchemy reads the same program to deploy and to test.

## The canonical example

[Effect-TS/cafe](https://github.com/Effect-TS/cafe) is a chat app from the Effect organization. Its README defines CAFE. [Sam Goodwin](/lore/sam-goodwin), who wrote Alchemy, built it. Maxwell Brown also commits to it.

It shows these patterns:

- `@cafe/api` holds the HTTP and [RPC](/skills/learn-rat-stack) schemas. It may import only `effect`, so the browser can import it safely. A lint rule enforces this.
- The Worker serves an Effect `HttpApi`. [PR #6](https://github.com/Effect-TS/cafe/pull/6) moves chat events to Effect RPC over a `Cloudflare.RpcDurableObject`, one per chat.
- The frontend is a Foldkit single-page app. Side effects are `Command.define` definitions. [PR #2](https://github.com/Effect-TS/cafe/pull/2) streamed socket frames with `Subscription.fromEvent`; PR #6 later replaced the socket with RPC.
- Story tests check update, Messages, and Commands. Scene tests drive the rendered view. Both are pure.
- Live tests deploy the Stack with `Test.make` from `alchemy/Test/Vitest`. The end-to-end test drives Chromium through Playwright.
- CI deploys one stage per pull request and destroys it when the pull request closes.
- `stacks/github.ts` is an Alchemy Stack that writes the CI Cloudflare credentials as repository secrets.
- Configuration comes from `effect/Config`. Its `AGENTS.md` forbids `process.env`.
- The repository carries the Foldkit agent skills.

## Other CAFE apps

| App | What it shows |
| --- | --- |
| [just-be-dev/effect-cloudflare-foldkit-template](https://github.com/just-be-dev/effect-cloudflare-foldkit-template) | A template with tooling and guardrails for Effect 4, Foldkit, and Alchemy 2 on Cloudflare. |
| [NigelThorne/foldkit-demo](https://github.com/NigelThorne/foldkit-demo) | Live shared sessions on Durable Objects with SQLite and hibernatable WebSockets. |
| [mwarger/corefour](https://github.com/mwarger/corefour) | A poster app with an Effect `HttpApi` Worker, Foldkit server rendering, and KV and R2 storage. |
| [Manzanita-Research/foldkit-dials](https://github.com/Manzanita-Research/foldkit-dials) | Live tuning controls for Foldkit apps. See the next section. |
| [Manzanita-Research/pleat](https://github.com/Manzanita-Research/pleat) | Typed styles for Foldkit and Effect 4. MIT. |
| [Effect-TS/slopcop](https://github.com/Effect-TS/slopcop) | Several Effect Workers with D1 and Queues, declared in one Alchemy Stack. |

Pleat treats a style as a value:

- Styles merge by fixed laws.
- Every rule compiles to atomic CSS when its module loads.
- Recipe variants are typed by Effect [Schema](/lore/schemas-define-the-boundary).
- A model that generates UI can choose styles, but it can never write CSS.

[Jem](https://github.com/jem-computer) at Manzanita Research builds actively in the CAFE space: Pleat, foldkit-dials, and [foldkit-native](https://github.com/Manzanita-Research/foldkit-native).

## foldkit-dials

[Manzanita-Research/foldkit-dials](https://github.com/Manzanita-Research/foldkit-dials) gives a Foldkit app live tuning controls, after DialKit. It is MIT licensed, at version 0.1.0.

- The dials are an Effect Schema.
- Every dial edit is a Message.
- Foldkit DevTools records each edit.
- Time travel replays it.
- Story and Scene tests can drive it.

Its demo deploys with Alchemy. A `stacks/github.ts` Stack bootstraps its CI credentials, as in cafe.

foldkit-dials is a clear example of the Foldkit rule that every change is a Message. A tool that follows the rule gets recording, replay, and tests from the runtime.

## Where rat-stack sits

rat-stack is a CAFE stack with [the fence](/lore/the-fence) around it. The table compares it with cafe at rat-stack commit `3fb103b`.

| Area | rat-stack | cafe |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Alchemy Worker shape | Class form: `Cloudflare.Worker<Mischief>()`, `Cloudflare.Workers.RpcWorker`, `Cloudflare.Website.Foldkit` | `Cloudflare.Worker`, `Cloudflare.RpcDurableObject`, `Cloudflare.Website.Foldkit` |
| Runtime tests | `alchemy/Test/Vitest` with fixture Workers in `apps/mischief/test/*-runtime.test.ts` | `Test.make` deploys the whole Stack; Playwright drives Chromium |
| API surface | One contract projected to RPC, HTTP, MCP, and CLI by `packages/capability` | Hand-written `HttpApi` and `RpcGroup` |
| Foldkit | `Runtime.makeApplication`, `Command.define`, `@foldkit/oxlint-plugin`, Story and Scene tests | The same, plus the Foldkit agent skills |
| Config | varlock `.env.schema` into Effect `Config`; no `process.env` in source | `effect/Config`; no `process.env` |
| Pull request stages | `scripts/deploy-preview.sh` deploys a Website and RpcBackend preview by hand; no live end-to-end test | CI deploys one stage per pull request, runs live tests, and destroys it on close |
| Tracing | `Cloudflare.Telemetry`, opt-in, off by default | Not enabled |

The largest difference is the API [surface](/lore/one-schema-three-surfaces). See [one capability, every surface](/lore/one-capability-every-surface) and [infrastructure as effects](/lore/infrastructure-as-effects).

